:4,"category":"riddle"},{"text":"What comes once in a minute, twice in a moment, but never in a thousand years?","format":"text","options":null,"answer":"m","alternatives":["the letter m","letter m"],"hint":"Look at the spelling","difficulty":4,"category":"riddle"},{"text":"I'm light as a feather, yet the strongest person can't hold me for five minutes. What am I?","format":"text","options":null,"answer":"breath","alternatives":["your breath","a breath"],"hint":"Inhale…","difficulty":4,"category":"riddle"},{"text":"What does this print?\ndef f(n):\n    return n if n < 2 else f(n - 1) + f(n - 2)\nprint(f(7))","format":"number","options":null,"answer":"13","alternatives":[],"hint":"Fibonacci: 0, 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, …","difficulty":5,"category":"coding"},{"text":"What does this print?\na = [1, 2, 3]\nb = a[:]\nb.append(4)\nprint(len(a), len(b))","format":"mcq","options":["3 4","4 4","3 3","4 3"],"answer":"0","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"coding"},{"text":"What does this print?\nx = 10\ndef change():\n    x = 5\nchange()\nprint(x)","format":"number","options":null,"answer":"10","alternatives":[],"hint":"The x inside the function is a different x","difficulty":5,"category":"coding"},{"text":"What does this print?\nprint({1, 2, 2, 3})","format":"mcq","options":["[1, 2, 3]","Error","{1, 2, 3}","{1, 2, 2, 3}"],"answer":"2","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"coding"},{"text":"What does this print?\nprint(len({\"a\": 1, \"b\": 2, \"a\": 3}))","format":"number","options":null,"answer":"2","alternatives":[],"hint":"A dictionary key can appear only once","difficulty":5,"category":"coding"},{"text":"What does this print?\nprint(\"Hello World\".split()[1][::-1])","format":"text","options":null,"answer":"dlroW","alternatives":[],"hint":"Take the second word, then reverse it","difficulty":5,"category":"coding"},{"text":"In JavaScript, what does this print?\nconsole.log(0.1 + 0.2 === 0.3)","format":"mcq","options":["Error","false","true","undefined"],"answer":"1","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"coding"},{"text":"What does this print?\nnums = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]\nprint(sum(n for n in nums if n % 3 == 0))","format":"number","options":null,"answer":"9","alternatives":[],"hint":"Only 3 and 6 count","difficulty":5,"category":"coding"},{"text":"What does this print?\nprint(type([]) == type(()))","format":"mcq","options":["True","Error","None","False"],"answer":"3","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"coding"},{"text":"What does this print?\ns = 0\nfor i in range(10):\n    if i == 5:\n        break\n    s += i\nprint(s)","format":"number","options":null,"answer":"10","alternatives":[],"hint":"0 + 1 + 2 + 3 + 4","difficulty":5,"category":"coding"},{"text":"What does this print?\nprint(\"abc\"[1:])","format":"text","options":null,"answer":"bc","alternatives":[],"hint":"Start from index 1","difficulty":5,"category":"coding"},{"text":"What does this print?\nprint(int(\"1010\", 2))","format":"number","options":null,"answer":"10","alternatives":[],"hint":"Read 1010 as binary","difficulty":5,"category":"coding"},{"text":"What does this print?\nprint([0] * 3)","format":"mcq","options":["[0]","[3]","0003","[0, 0, 0]"],"answer":"3","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"coding"},{"text":"Fix the bug: this crashes. Which line prints the last number instead?\nnums = [1, 2, 3]\nprint(nums[3])","format":"mcq","options":["print(nums[2])","print(nums(3))","print(nums{3})","print(nums.3)"],"answer":"0","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"coding"},{"text":"What does this print?\nprint(len(str(2 ** 10)))","format":"number","options":null,"answer":"4","alternatives":[],"hint":"2 ** 10 is 1024","difficulty":5,"category":"coding"},{"text":"What does an HTTP 500 error mean?","format":"mcq","options":["You are not logged in","The page loaded fine","Something broke on the server","The page was moved"],"answer":"2","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"tech"},{"text":"What does API stand for?","format":"text","options":null,"answer":"Application Programming Interface","alternatives":["application program interface"],"hint":"A is for Application","difficulty":5,"category":"tech"},{"text":"Which sorting method keeps swapping neighbouring items until the list is in order?","format":"mcq","options":["Bubble sort","Merge sort","Quick sort","Heap sort"],"answer":"0","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"tech"},{"text":"How many layers does the OSI network model have?","format":"number","options":null,"answer":"7","alternatives":[],"hint":"Same as the days of the week","difficulty":5,"category":"tech"},{"text":"On average, how long does looking up a key in a hash map take?","format":"mcq","options":["O(log n)","O(n log n)","O(1)","O(n)"],"answer":"2","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"tech"},{"text":"Which company first created the Java language?","format":"text","options":null,"answer":"Sun Microsystems","alternatives":["sun","sun micro systems"],"hint":"Named after a star","difficulty":5,"category":"tech"},{"text":"Which of these is NOT a standard HTTP method?","format":"mcq","options":["FETCH","GET","POST","DELETE"],"answer":"0","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"tech"},{"text":"What is the hexadecimal number FF in decimal?","format":"number","options":null,"answer":"255","alternatives":[],"hint":"One less than 256","difficulty":5,"category":"tech"},{"text":"What do we call fake messages that trick you into giving away your password?","format":"text","options":null,"answer":"phishing","alternatives":["phishing attack","fishing"],"hint":"Sounds like catching fish","difficulty":5,"category":"tech"},{"text":"What does \"open source\" software mean?","format":"mcq","options":["It never has bugs","It only runs on Linux","Nobody is allowed to change it","Its code is public for anyone to read and improve"],"answer":"3","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"tech"},{"text":"Who gave the theory of relativity?","format":"mcq","options":["Albert Einstein","Isaac Newton","Stephen Hawking","Galileo Galilei"],"answer":"0","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"science"},{"text":"What is the capital of Brazil?","format":"text","options":null,"answer":"Brasilia","alternatives":[],"hint":"Not Rio de Janeiro!","difficulty":5,"category":"geography"},{"text":"How many hearts does an octopus have?","format":"number","options":null,"answer":"3","alternatives":[],"hint":"More than one, fewer than five","difficulty":5,"category":"science"},{"text":"Which Indian mathematician is linked to the famous number 1729?","format":"mcq","options":["Aryabhata","Bhaskara","Brahmagupta","Srinivasa Ramanujan"],"answer":"3","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"history"},{"text":"In which year did the Constitution of India come into effect?","format":"number","options":null,"answer":"1950","alternatives":[],"hint":"26 January, a few years after independence","difficulty":5,"category":"history"},{"text":"Which planet spins tipped over on its side?","format":"mcq","options":["Neptune","Uranus","Venus","Mars"],"answer":"1","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"science"},{"text":"Which metal is a liquid at room temperature?","format":"text","options":null,"answer":"mercury","alternatives":[],"hint":"Also the planet closest to the Sun","difficulty":5,"category":"science"},{"text":"How many players from one team are on a volleyball court?","format":"number","options":null,"answer":"6","alternatives":[],"hint":"Half a dozen","difficulty":5,"category":"sports"},{"text":"Which is the smallest country in the world?","format":"mcq","options":["Vatican City","Monaco","Malta","Maldives"],"answer":"0","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"geography"},{"text":"In which city were the first modern Olympic Games held, in 1896?","format":"text","options":null,"answer":"Athens","alternatives":[],"hint":"Capital of Greece","difficulty":5,"category":"history"},{"text":"Who was the first Indian to win a Nobel Prize?","format":"mcq","options":["Mother Teresa","Amartya Sen","Rabindranath Tagore","C. V. Raman"],"answer":"2","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"history"},{"text":"In which year did Chandrayaan-3 land on the Moon?","format":"number","options":null,"answer":"2023","alternatives":[],"hint":"Just a few years ago","difficulty":5,"category":"science"},{"text":"Which is the largest country in the world by area?","format":"text","options":null,"answer":"Russia","alternatives":[],"hint":"It spans Europe and Asia","difficulty":5,"category":"geography"},{"text":"Which of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World still stands?","format":"mcq","options":["The Lighthouse of Alexandria","The Great Pyramid of Giza","The Hanging Gardens of Babylon","The Colossus of Rhodes"],"answer":"1","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"history"},{"text":"How many time zones does India officially use?","format":"number","options":null,"answer":"1","alternatives":[],"hint":"Think of IST","difficulty":5,"category":"geography"},{"text":"Which Indian scientist won the Nobel Prize for the scattering of light?","format":"text","options":null,"answer":"C V Raman","alternatives":["raman","cv raman","c.v. raman","c. v. raman","chandrasekhara venkata raman"],"hint":"The effect is named after him","difficulty":5,"category":"history"},{"text":"Which part is called \"the powerhouse of the cell\"?","format":"mcq","options":["Mitochondria","Nucleus","Ribosome","Cell wall"],"answer":"0","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"science"},{"text":"How many sides does a decagon have?","format":"number","options":null,"answer":"10","alternatives":[],"hint":"Like a decade","difficulty":5,"category":"math"},{"text":"Which famous ship sank in 1912 after hitting an iceberg?","format":"text","options":null,"answer":"Titanic","alternatives":["the titanic","rms titanic"],"hint":"A famous film too","difficulty":5,"category":"history"},{"text":"Which space agency launched Mangalyaan to Mars?","format":"mcq","options":["NASA","DRDO","ESA","ISRO"],"answer":"3","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"science"},{"text":"What is 17 × 6?","format":"number","options":null,"answer":"102","alternatives":[],"hint":"17 × 5 is 85","difficulty":5,"category":"math"},{"text":"Which blood group is known as the universal donor?","format":"text","options":null,"answer":"O negative","alternatives":["o-","o neg","onegative","o -ve","o-ve","o negative blood"],"hint":"The letter O","difficulty":5,"category":"science"},{"text":"Which emperor gave up war after the Kalinga war?","format":"mcq","options":["Chandragupta Maurya","Harsha","Ashoka","Akbar"],"answer":"2","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"history"},{"text":"Which word is spelled wrong in every dictionary?","format":"text","options":null,"answer":"wrong","alternatives":[],"hint":"Read the question again","difficulty":5,"category":"riddle"},{"text":"If two's company and three's a crowd, what are four and five?","format":"number","options":null,"answer":"9","alternatives":[],"hint":"Just add them","difficulty":5,"category":"riddle"},{"text":"I speak without a mouth and hear without ears. What am I?","format":"text","options":null,"answer":"echo","alternatives":["an echo"],"hint":"Shout in a valley","difficulty":5,"category":"riddle"},{"text":"A bat and a ball cost ₹110 together. The bat costs ₹100 more than the ball. How much is the ball?","format":"mcq","options":["₹100","₹1","₹5","₹10"],"answer":"2","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"riddle"},{"text":"A snail climbs 3 m up a 10 m well each day and slips back 2 m each night. On which day does it reach the top?","format":"number","options":null,"answer":"8","alternatives":[],"hint":"On the last day it doesn't slip back","difficulty":5,"category":"riddle"},{"text":"Which place completes the meme \"One does not simply walk into…\"?","format":"mcq","options":["Mordor","Hogwarts","Narnia","Gotham"],"answer":"0","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"meme"},{"text":"What is always in front of you but can't be seen?","format":"text","options":null,"answer":"future","alternatives":["the future"],"hint":"Tomorrow is part of it","difficulty":5,"category":"riddle"},{"text":"In the \"This is fine\" meme, where is the dog sitting?","format":"mcq","options":["In a spaceship","In a traffic jam","In a room on fire","In a swimming pool"],"answer":"2","alternatives":[],"hint":null,"difficulty":5,"category":"meme"},{"text":"How many times can you subtract 5 from 25?","format":"number","options":null,"answer":"1","alternatives":[],"hint":"After the first time, it isn't 25 any more","difficulty":5,"category":"riddle"},{"text":"What has cities but no houses, forests but no trees, and water but no fish?","format":"text","options":null,"answer":"map","alternatives":["a map"],"hint":"Treasure hunters love one","difficulty":5,"category":"riddle"}]$bank$::jsonb) q
